<template><div class="stack"><div class="split grow"><div class="col"><h2>Reference fidelity</h2><p class="formula blue">PSNR = 10 log₁₀(MAX² / MSE)</p><p>Higher PSNR means smaller pixel error against the recorded target.</p><p class="formula">SSIM(Ô, T)</p><p>SSIM compares luminance, contrast and structural similarity. Record preprocessing, image range and aggregation.</p><p class="note">Neither metric directly measures whether a user prefers an alternative edit.</p></div><div class="col"><h2>Candidate selection</h2><div class="node"><h3>Top-1 · inference</h3><p>Select a candidate without access to the query target.</p></div><div class="node"><h3>Best-of-K · evaluation only</h3><p>Use the query target to score the best among the first K candidates.</p></div><p class="formula small">score = maxₖ metric(candidateₖ, T)</p><p class="note warning">Best-of-K measures candidate coverage. It is not an available runtime selection rule.</p></div></div><p class="small muted">Report PSNR and SSIM independently; do not assume the same candidate maximises both without a documented evaluation implementation.</p></div></template>
